eady to roll policin acquired the  mechanical components like axles and the  engine from Porsche the 110 horsepower  engine swiftly carried his thousand  kilogram creation to a speed of 200  kilometers an hour a respectable  performance for the early 1970s in 1975  the Baron Dino got the blessings of the  state inspectors policin explains that  he was in constant contact with the  state inspection point in cologne the  only one that is authorized to deal with  prototypes he had tailored the interior  of the barely one metre high Baron Dino  to his own one meter 70 height and  located the instruments in the center  console to save space the two liter  6-cylinder boxer engine from the Porsche  911 is mounted in the rear unusual are  the auxiliary instruments in the engine  compartment policin calls it a service  panel and it's unique to the bear Adina  it comes in very handy when he services  the engines he can even start the engine  from the back when he synchronizes the  carburetors he put all the instruments  needed for the 911 engine in the rear  such as the oil pressure and temperature  gauges don't meter  Alison even build various model versions  of his bear adeno besides the fastback  there's a notch back with a different  hatch and if so desired he can even  convert the sports car into a breezy  roadster the convertible is version 3  and policin sees a bright future for the  bear Adina short thought safe he says  he's got plans for modernizing the car  to make it attractive to today's drivers  it's not a matter of copying the now  vintage sports car but of redesigning it  with cutting-edge components and  technology son on mama says an auto for  now Afghanistan with Madonna technique  Collison is on the lookout for partners  willing to contribute to the new bear  Adina that would make Johannes Paulson's  dream come true to see the spirit of the  borough Dino live on
 

